mission "The False Beacon"
    name "The False Beacon"
    description "Silence a false lighthouse signal that has been drawing ships onto a reef at night."
    source "Port Royal"
    destination "Last Light"
    reward 1720
    speaker offer "Warden Sloane"
    speaker visit "Warden Sloane"
    speaker complete "Warden Sloane"
    to offer
        has "A Bargain with Black Jack: done"
    objective kills 2
    battlefield "False Beacon Reach" 16600 2600
    enemy "Rook's Vanguard"
    enemy "Rook's Second"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Warden Sloane has laid several wreck reports beside a chart of the reef. Every ship struck the same stretch of stone, and every master swore they had followed the lighthouse.`
            `Sloane taps the lighthouse mark. "The light is false. Someone has been showing ships a safe channel that does not exist, and the reef has been collecting the wreckage. I want the signal stopped before another crew follows it."`
            choice
                `"If there is a truth to find, I will help find it."`
                    accept
                `"What does this have to do with the old expedition?"`
                    goto details
                `"I will not chase a secret on promises alone."`
                    close
            label details
                `Sloane opens an older chart. "The expedition's route passes close to this coast. If someone is altering lights as well as charts, the false beacon may be part of the same effort. Silence it and bring me the signal record."`
                choice
                    `"Very well. Let us bring this into the open."`
                        accept
                    `"I have heard enough. I must be on my way."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The False Beacon. Silence a false lighthouse signal that has been drawing ships onto a reef at night."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Last Light, Sloane compares the recovered signal with the proper sequence. The false beacon has been drawing ships onto the reef at night. "One more night and there would have been another wreck," Sloane says. "We have stopped it."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Sloane checks the lamp before closing the logbook. "The light is true again, and the signal record is safe. The sea is dangerous enough without someone moving the shore with a lantern. You have done these waters a service."`
        log "Completed The False Beacon. Received 1720 gold. Silence a false lighthouse signal that has been drawing ships onto a reef at night."
